<title>HONG KONG: Goodwill interim net rises sharply.</title>
<headline>Goodwill interim net rises sharply.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   18.4   vs 6.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    3.0    vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs nil (see note)</p>
<p>    Net			    42.60  vs 6.82</p>
<p>    Turnover		     315.11 vs 13.83</p>
<p>    Company name		 Goodwill Investment (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 30 to October 4</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 11</p>
<p>NOTE - A property investment and development and financial services firm.</p>
<p>Comparative exceptional loss of HK$749,000 was reclassified as normal loss to be consistent with 1995's audited results.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
